{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children","id":541743,"title":"Beast: Can Beast's have children?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-05T15:22:23-07:00","id":541743,"title":"Beast: Can Beast's have children?","content":"My question is in two parts.<br /> <br /> 1. Can Beasts have children?<br /> <br /> 2. What are the children? Beasts? Or are they a lesser template of some sort because they were not spawned directly from the Dark Mother?<br /> <br /> I haven't seen anything in the book that regards my questions looking either manually or using the search functions, although it does not help that they are called &quot;The Dark <b>CHILDREN</b>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:24:16-07:00","id":541757,"title":"","content":"1) I see no reason why not.<br /> <br /> 2) I'd assume they're mortals, abet I'd probably argue that they're far more likely to develop Supernatural Merits than normal people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:35:42-07:00","id":541765,"title":"","content":"cough<b>LUCID DREAMER</b>cough<br /> <br /> Seriously though, idk...... mortal? You go from a giant able to throw a size 300 something object(Saturn/Jupiter for reference) to MORTAL.......really?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:49:18-07:00","id":541775,"title":"","content":"Unless something is preventing the individual Beast from having offspring then there is nothing that stops them from procreating. In fact one of the fluff pieces in the pdf is from a Beast and it includes it wondering which parent ,the other apparently was a hero, their daughters took after.<br /> <br /> As for what the kids are the pdf says that being one of the Children does not follow a bloodline, so it is possible that the offspring of a Beast could become a Beast this is by no means certainty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:52:24-07:00","id":541777,"title":"","content":"So the children really are mortal?.............WOW..........<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T16:30:46-07:00","id":541805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=541777#post541777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the children really are mortal?.............WOW..........</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably like what Zealous said and they have a higher probability of ending up with some sort of supernatural awareness. To restate the kids could turn out to be Beasts it just isn't a certainty, I imagine this to allow easy avoidance of what happens if a Beast were to have children with one of the other splats that can have kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T16:36:10-07:00","id":541826,"title":"","content":"I assume progeny of Begotten has higher chance of becoming the Beast herself by heritage. &quot;Do you remeber the way great unt Matilda got on those wierd nights? You have the same glare in the eyes, my dear.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-05-2015, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T17:13:34-07:00","id":541855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=541826#post541826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume progeny of Begotten has higher chance of becoming the Beast herself by heritage. &amp;quot;Do you remeber the way great unt Matilda got on those wierd nights? You have the same glare in the eyes, my dear.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It is specifically said that parentage has nothing to do with it. Also, you don't &quot;become&quot; a Beast. Your either born a Beast or you aren't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theo