"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:24:54-07:00","id":542258,"title":"","content":"I love the way this conversation has gone, please continue.<br /> <br /> But, in all seriousness I think that there should be some sort of minor template for when <b>something</b> does get passed down to a Beast's children, whatever the cause. For several reasons:<br /> <br /> 1. Because it seems somewhat likely that there could be about a 10 percent chance of something getting passed down, not good odds maybe, but better than getting hit with lightning and that seems to happen all the time.(Yes, number pulled out of thin air, but it does seem possible.)<br /> <br /> 2. Powergap. Beast-Mortal, Werewolf-Wolfblooded, Vampire-Ghoul, Mage-Proximi; do you see where I'm going with this? These other things have the ability to pass down a lesser version of themselves. Lesser because what is being passed down is further from the source, the origin of power. Why not the Beasts?<br /> <br /> Am I really that far off base here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6154,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","user":"DeathMonkee","date":". 06-06-2015, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T01:29:18-07:00","id":542387,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'd go with Night Terrors- Goetia (since that's what astral spirits are going to be called in second edition) that aren't powerful enough to incarnate into humans. So either free floating goetia or in animal form, goetia that can manifest their true selves inside a Beast's lair, or go traveling with the beast's soul on a hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T02:23:32-07:00","id":542401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=542258#post542258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the way this conversation has gone, please continue.<br /> <br /> But, in all seriousness I think that there should be some sort of minor template for when <b>something</b> does get passed down to a Beast's children, whatever the cause. For several reasons:<br /> <br /> 1. Because it seems somewhat likely that there could be about a 10 percent chance of something getting passed down, not good odds maybe, but better than getting hit with lightning and that seems to happen all the time.(Yes, number pulled out of thin air, but it does seem possible.)<br /> <br /> 2. Powergap. Beast-Mortal, Werewolf-Wolfblooded, Vampire-Ghoul, Mage-Proximi; do you see where I'm going with this? These other things have the ability to pass down a lesser version of themselves. Lesser because what is being passed down is further from the source, the origin of power. Why not the Beasts?<br /> <br /> Am I really that far off base here?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say - yes. Why do we want to shoehorn EVERY splat into &quot;he's able to create weaker versions of himself&quot; ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And by Beasts terms, every other splat is a &quot;weaker version of themselves&quot; :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T02:55:47-07:00","id":542407,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://orig09.deviantart.net/ce15/f/2015/054/b/f/not_all_damsels_are_distressed_by_golentan-d8j98wr.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Curse this thread for making me share this!</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Can't post pictures, even spoiled ones. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T03:39:41-07:00","id":542421,"title":"","content":"Who would <i>want </i>to get intimate with a beast? Sharing a bed with a namtaru can't be awfully comfortable. Or safe. On the topic of minor templates, there are other splats that have normal children- Changelings, Mummies, Geists, Mages and Prometheans all have 'normal' kids, or children with some supernatural merits at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T03:48:18-07:00","id":542426,"title":"","content":"I think it's hinted that Beast's &quot;minor splat&quot; is, well, <i>Heroes. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T04:09:51-07:00","id":542433,"title":"","content":"Zeus is the son of Cronus the Titan, after all... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's stated that Zeus was the Hero of the story between him and Typhon in the Inheritance section, after all... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T06:21:28-07:00","id":542487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=542421#post542421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who would <i>want </i>to get intimate with a beast? Sharing a bed with a namtaru can't be awfully comfortable. Or safe. On the topic of minor templates, there are other splats that have normal children- Changelings, Mummies, Geists, Mages and Prometheans all have 'normal' kids, or children with some supernatural merits at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell that to the people who get in bed with vampires or prometheans as well as werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:41:08-07:00","id":542611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children#post541743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is in two parts.<br /> <br /> 1. Can Beasts have children?<br /> <br /> 2. What are the children? Beasts? Or are they a lesser template of some sort because they were not spawned directly from the Dark Mother?<br /> <br /> I haven't seen anything in the book that regards my questions looking either manually or using the search functions, although it does not help that they are called &quot;The Dark <b>CHILDREN</b>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The way the pdf described it, any human can become a Beast, which indicates that it's something along the lines of Werewolf. You're born and raised human, but you don't quite have a human soul. Then one day things change and you find out what you really are. So yes, Beasts should be able to have children, but there's no guarantee they'll be Beasts as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> The pdf also says that the transformation into a Beast <i>starts</i> <i>early on</i>, usually around childhood.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, on a side note. Beasts are &quot;mortal&quot; too. It even comments on this in the pdf saying that Beasts do grow old over time, although a significantly powerful Beast can live for a very long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-06-2015, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:23:05-07:00","id":542917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=541765#post541765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cough<b>LUCID DREAMER</b>cough<br /> <br /> Seriously though, idk...... mortal? You go from a giant able to throw a size 300 something object(Saturn/Jupiter for reference) to MORTAL.......really?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing supernatural about a Beast's body when they aren't using an atavism. I don't know why their offspring would be supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T15:47:11-07:00","id":543148,"title":"","content":"Realistically? Their children would become Heroes. Think about it. Day in, day out, next to a Beast for some two decades and you want to tell me that the Beast never screws up and goes on a rampage and starts converting his/her own family into Heroes? Maybe it's possible. But this is the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T16:09:43-07:00","id":543182,"title":"","content":"That sounds right. One of the example Heroes was a housewife who turned Hero after her son turned into a Beast, the other way around is probably more likely.<br /> <br /> Beastdom doesn't seem to have any bearing on genetics, but like someone above said, it might be interesting plot-wise for you to have some relative Beast, but the rules don't really support that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:06:54-07:00","id":543335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=543148#post543148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Realistically? Their children would become Heroes. Think about it. Day in, day out, next to a Beast for some two decades and you want to tell me that the Beast never screws up and goes on a rampage and starts converting his/her own family into Heroes? Maybe it's possible. But this is the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well it says that prior to their homecoming, a Beast is plagued with recurring nightmares their whole life, and the process begins as early as childhood. So really it could go either way between Hero and Beast, depending upon how the child responds to their affliction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T21:47:47-07:00","id":543465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=543335#post543335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it says that prior to their homecoming, a Beast is plagued with recurring nightmares their whole life, and the process begins as early as childhood. So really it could go either way between Hero and Beast, depending upon how the child responds to their affliction.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> Fair enough. Not where my mind went but now the story fodder it inspires...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T18:54:28-07:00","id":674782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=542387#post542387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm, I'd go with Night Terrors- Goetia (since that's what astral spirits are going to be called in second edition) that aren't powerful enough to incarnate into humans. So either free floating goetia or in animal form, goetia that can manifest their true selves inside a Beast's lair, or go traveling with the beast's soul on a hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually made me think of a Roger Zelazney novel, <b>Lord Demon</b>. The &quot;Demon&quot; race (which actually remind me a lot of true fae from <i>Changeling: the Dreaming</i>) are powerful, brilliant, unearthly beings . . .not entirely dissimilar to the Begotten. But they're not breeding true - too often, their kids are these runty/inbred/retarded freaks, with none of the power or majesty of their parents.<br /> <br /> Might be an idea for the result of two Souls/Horrors getting it on - particularly if you want a &quot;mother of monsters&quot; concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T20:55:03-07:00","id":674910,"title":"","content":"From the Ugallu introduction:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\">The Simurgh has a special place in Ugallu thought as one of the few Beasts of legend known for<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family: \"> its mercy. The young prince Zal was revealed as a Beast as a child and left to die in the<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family: \"> wilderness. The Simurgh took him in and taught him the ways of magic. Returning to the world<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family: \"> of humanity, Zal was greeted as a savior, performing great works of medicine and even saving<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family: \"> his wife<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\">\u2019<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\">s life during childbirth. The son, however, became a Hero; while he spared his father,<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family: \"> his own child was not so lucky.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>So, yes, Beasts' children can be Heroes, and vice versa!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T02:52:24-07:00","id":675079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=542421#post542421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who would <i>want </i>to get intimate with a beast? Sharing a bed with a namtaru can't be awfully comfortable. Or safe. On the topic of minor templates, there are other splats that have normal children- Changelings, Mummies, Geists, Mages and Prometheans all have 'normal' kids, or children with some supernatural merits at best.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If the internet has taught me anything, its that there are quite a lot of people out there who are into some kinky shit that makes Beast seem tame by comparison! Also remember that Beasts can enter people's dreams, similar to Changelings. There's plenty of ways they can seduce / coerce a human into bed without the human even realizing what's going on.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Changelings having kids, the general rule about them is that most of them are infertile. Like only 1 to 10% of their world wide population can still have kids and even then, they're born mortal. With 2nd edition coming up, Fae Touched will be people who made a promise with a Changeling before they were taken away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-26-2015, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T03:10:47-07:00","id":675085,"title":"","content":"The Makara are all over the Siren gig. <br /> <br /> Lol, tentacles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T05:33:10-07:00","id":675137,"title":"","content":"This idea that a Beast's body is not supernatural outside of their power usage and therefore consequently their offspring would be mortal is strange.<br /> <br /> A Demon's body is completely mortal at all times when inhabiting their Cover, they literally tell the universal base code to physically replace them with a human body so as to achieve this. Yet, Demons and Angels both make Offspring quite regularly.<br /> <br /> Maybe we'll get more information on this when Beast is released, but, given that a person can live their entire lives without ever properly awakening their Beast and thus becoming one of the Begotten it seems reasonable to suggest that Beasts beget other Beasts, but that doesn't always mean they turn around and face their Horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T05:53:37-07:00","id":675150,"title":"","content":"The difference is that a demon's human body is fake. The universe is being told that the demon is really a human, but it's not perfect. It can glitch. That effectively what an Offspring is. A glitch in reality. <br /> <br /> Beasts, on the other hand, have an entirely real human shell. Their monstrous form exists on another plane of reality entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T06:02:46-07:00","id":675166,"title":"","content":"I'd Say they could have Children... And they'd be Mortal unless the Beast is an Incarnate... in which case I'd Say they are Born Beasts... Maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T10:20:43-07:00","id":675349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=675079#post675079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Changelings having kids, the general rule about them is that most of them are infertile. Like only 1 to 10% of their world wide population can still have kids and even then, they're born mortal. With 2nd edition coming up, Fae Touched will be people who made a promise with a Changeling before they were taken away.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fairly sure the infertility thing was dropped in 2e changeling.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T11:24:15-07:00","id":675451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=675137#post675137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Demon's body is completely mortal at all times when inhabiting their Cover, they literally tell the universal base code to physically replace them with a human body so as to achieve this. Yet, Demons and Angels both make Offspring quite regularly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels don't, but setting that aside, the Unchained throw up enough metaphysical glitches even at high Cover that people knowledgeable about the occult can pick up on it with focus, their human life is the first thing to get saddled with techno-folkloric manifestations of their true identity if they don't immediately draw the attentions of the higher power that regularly makes Bigfoots by accident, their supernatural aesthetic resonates with things like genetics and pharmaceuticals and other things that have an impact on childbirth, and above all else having your children be a potential risk to your Cover is in-theme for the game, as is the notion that the Machine might exploit the profane merger of occult programming and human fertility that Offspring and Fractals represent.<br /> <br /> Demonic subterfuge is very good in places, but it's far from airtight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-23-2015, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T23:11:25-07:00","id":678589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=675451#post675451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angels don't, but setting that aside, the Unchained throw up enough metaphysical glitches even at high Cover that people knowledgeable about the occult can pick up on it with focus, their human life is the first thing to get saddled with techno-folkloric manifestations of their true identity if they don't immediately draw the attentions of the higher power that regularly makes Bigfoots by accident, their supernatural aesthetic resonates with things like genetics and pharmaceuticals and other things that have an impact on childbirth, and above all else having your children be a potential risk to your Cover is in-theme for the game, as is the notion that the Machine might exploit the profane merger of occult programming and human fertility that Offspring and Fractals represent.<br /> <br /> Demonic subterfuge is very good in places, but it's far from airtight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree, yet the same can be said for a beast. A beast's child could be threatened by a Hero. See: Beowulf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T23:33:27-07:00","id":678592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=678589#post678589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't disagree, yet the same can be said for a beast. A beast's child could be threatened by a Hero. See: Beowulf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Grendel being a monster whose mother is also a monster is kind of incidental to the fact that the Horror acts independently of the Beast's human body outside the Lair and that the vast majority of supernatural beings capable of biological fertility do not consistently pass down even a partial connection to their magical nature; the exception with the most regularity is, in fact, demon-blooded \u2014 more regular examples are the stuff of true-breeding archspells or very persistent eugenics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T01:19:52-07:00","id":678630,"title":"","content":"At the risk of resurrecting the original topic.<br /> <br /> Can a Beast Incarnate have children?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T07:12:42-07:00","id":678982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=678630#post678630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of resurrecting the original topic.<br /> <br /> Can a Beast Incarnate have children?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why wouldn't they? They're physical beings, instead of residing in the dream world. Unless they're sexually androgynous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T08:34:00-07:00","id":679054,"title":"","content":"I'd go with yes they can have offspring, who can be either mortal or Beast, but not a lesser template, because what defines Beasts strikes me as fairly all or nothing. However, mortal children will have an unusually high chance to pick up supernatural traits like Unseen Sense or Psychic Merits (or being Heroes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T11:24:14-07:00","id":679195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=678982#post678982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't they? They're physical beings, instead of residing in the dream world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're unique. Genetically, they don't seem human. But they also don't seem compatible with each other.<br /> <br /> Based on the 'first' edition, at least, I'm waiting for my book to check on the updates.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T13:19:28-07:00","id":679295,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, I could totally see children of beasts getting Unseen Sense: Goetia. That would be pretty trippy for the kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T07:20:35-08:00","id":790848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=542421#post542421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who would <i>want </i>to get intimate with a beast? Sharing a bed with a namtaru can't be awfully comfortable. Or safe. On the topic of minor templates, there are other splats that have normal children- Changelings, Mummies, Geists, Mages and Prometheans all have 'normal' kids, or children with some supernatural merits at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until they go through The New Dawn and become human, Prometheans cannot have children in the biological sense. As for sharing a bed with a Namtaru, remember that unless they are using their Atavisms or within their Liar, a Beast looks completely human. It's quite possible for a Namtaru to be very attractive\u200b; indeed, I think that might be a good concept for a character: A pretty face hides an ugly Soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T07:55:15-08:00","id":790857,"title":"","content":"There's lots of things either way. I think of it like genetics. There's the potential someone's kid will have the &quot;supernatural&quot; gene, and some kind of psychic ability, or something sadistic hungers that echo their parents, and the potential to be completely normal. It all depends on how the genes shake out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T09:49:07-08:00","id":790893,"title":"","content":"This splat has nothing to do with Goetic Daemons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T10:39:01-08:00","id":790919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=790893#post790893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This splat has nothing to do with Goetic Daemons.</div> </div> </div> </div>This splat is centered on powers drawn from a region of the Astral Realms, whose occupants as a whole are known as goetia in Mage 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T11:53:35-08:00","id":790956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=678592#post678592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grendel being a monster whose mother is also a monster is kind of incidental to the fact that the Horror acts independently of the Beast's human body outside the Lair and that the vast majority of supernatural beings capable of biological fertility do not consistently pass down even a partial connection to their magical nature; the exception with the most regularity is, in fact, demon-blooded \u2014 more regular examples are the stuff of true-breeding archspells or very persistent eugenics.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds more authoritative than it is. We already know that we'll be getting Dhampyrs in the future. Wolf-Blooded are a major thing (and unlike Dhampyrs and Offspring can be promoted to full splatdom). Given its strong focus on family, Beast needed to pay at least 500 words of attention to this issue. <br /> <br /> That said, it seems likely that most Beasts that have children can expect them to be mortal because Beasts are mostly mortal. That these children can become heroes under the correct conditions seems like a no-brainer for the storyteller. Storytellers and troupes looking for something more (perhaps along the lines of Stigmatics or Wolf-Blooded) might simply make up a new supernatural merit for mortals that gives them Kinship with Beasts that they are related to by blood (sometimes blood is important and sometimes blood does tell). Make this a merit that is compatible with being a ghoul, stigmatic, wolf-blooded, etc. and you have the makings of a really interesting chronicle (particularly for the person playing the ghoul (etc.)).<br /> <br /> It would have also been interesting if the game had confronted the mother of monsters character concept strait on by providing some kind of Lair Trait that simulates broods of baby horrors that the character's horror produces and populates its Lair with. The ante could be upped if these Lair 0 horrors could prowl the Hive looking for folks with the merit described above to be used as a means for getting out in the world (using the possess -&gt; control -&gt; claim mechanics). These things could have taken up much of the space currently consumed by the rather out-of-place ephemera rules that don't really add anything to the game's text.<br /> <br /> There was really no need to just out and say no in the book when these things are really just a matter of troupe / storyteller preferences. But sometimes opportunities get missed. It isn't like Beast is a bad game by any stretch of the imagination. It's just not as perfect as V:tR or W:tF. (And yeah, some of us have players that like playing mortals that genetically connect to a game's core content. Meeting their needs isn't insurmountable using hacks similar to the ones suggested above.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:32:27-08:00","id":790997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=790848#post790848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Until they go through The New Dawn and become human, Prometheans cannot have children in the biological sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect, actually. Pre-Dawn Prometheans can have children, either by mating with humans or by mating with each other. It's just rare to the point of being regarded as miraculous by Prometheans - although that might have to do with the fact that Scions are completely immune to Disquiet and can see through the Promethean &quot;mask&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T13:35:56-08:00","id":791055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=790997#post790997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incorrect, actually. Pre-Dawn Prometheans can have children, either by mating with humans or by mating with each other. It's just rare to the point of being regarded as miraculous by Prometheans - although that might have to do with the fact that Scions are completely immune to Disquiet and can see through the Promethean &quot;mask&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, with regards to Prometheans I always thought it would make sense if they had a ghoul-like demi-splat that simulated their early attempts at making another Promethean (still, I think, a requirement of their Pilgrimage) or to give players an option for a puppet who puppeteers character concept. Like a Promethean they'd be something made but cause like twice as much Disquiet. Like a Wolf-blooded they could be promoted into a &quot;full splat&quot; under certain conditions but only into a Pandoran.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T15:52:04-08:00","id":791132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=790893#post790893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This splat has nothing to do with Goetic Daemons.</div> </div> </div> </div> They have EVERYTHING to do with Goetics. The Horror is pretty much is a goetic entity itself. The game may be severely lacking in information for traveling through the Astral and its inhabitants, but that is something that absolutely does happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=790997#post790997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incorrect, actually. Pre-Dawn Prometheans can have children, either by mating with humans or by mating with each other. It's just rare to the point of being regarded as miraculous by Prometheans - although that might have to do with the fact that Scions are completely immune to Disquiet and can see through the Promethean &quot;mask&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> We've been told that Scions don't exist in 2e promethean. Fairly sure that Mangle is right if we're talking 2e only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T19:45:21-08:00","id":791238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=791132#post791132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They have EVERYTHING to do with Goetics. The Horror is pretty much is a goetic entity itself. The game may be severely lacking in information for traveling through the Astral and its inhabitants, but that is something that absolutely does happen.<br /> <br /> We've been told that Scions don't exist in 2e promethean. Fairly sure that Mangle is right if we're talking 2e only.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to ignore the &quot;No Scion&quot; decree at my table; it removes too many stories.<br /> <br /> But since I am yet to comment on the primary topic in this thread my position is as follows; the Begotten are biologically human, thus can &amp; do reproduce as humans, with the children also being human. If you want your baby to be a Beast, best Devour her.<br /> The conflict works fairly well for a splat focused on family, as opposed to say a game like Promethean which includes a significant theme of rejection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T20:27:48-08:00","id":791260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=790956#post790956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds more authoritative than it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Most supernaturals don't as-a-rule provide any magical connection to their offspring&quot; is not a statement on anything other than the baseline presentation of the games and what metaphysical plothooks they do not universally offer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We already know that we'll be getting Dhampyrs in the future. </div> </div> </div>We also know next to nothing about 2e dhampyr aside from their likely difference in handling from 1e dhampyr. Also, see &quot;capable of biological fertility.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wolf-Blooded are a major thing (and unlike Dhampyrs and Offspring can be promoted to full splatdom). </div> </div> </div>See &quot;do not <b>consistently</b> pass down even a partial connection.&quot; Wolf-blooded are even less consistently genetically-derived in 2e than they were in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-22-2015, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:15:30-08:00","id":791288,"title":"","content":"Furthering the line of thought that wants the Children of Beasts to be 'magic', I feel something akin to Cambions (Dancers in the Dusk pg 37; CtL 1st) would be more appropriate than 'Beast jr.'<br /> <br /> At my table, such a child would need to be conceived at the Beast's Lair...And I would not allow a 'situation' to occur whilst the Horror is on a Hunger Walkabout.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, normal human children are the order of the day; just imagine you come home tired from work and yet again you've failed to feed the horror inside you properly. After a quick dinner, you put the kids to bed and cuddle up to watch a movie with your partner, but your so exhausted you can barely keep your ey-*yawns*...<br /> Suddenly you hear your youngest screaming. You and your partner bolt up and rush to the little one's room. It seems the poor child had a nightmare. But when your baby describe the monster in their dreams your heart drops...<br /> Your partner smiles as zhe turns to you and says you should handle it. After all you had those sort of night terrors before, when you were younger.<br /> Problem is, you are your own child's nightmare, the monster who hunted them.<br /> <br /> I feel the above is a very strong story element, even if it is only a rumour one of your players hears about rather than experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T23:36:45-08:00","id":791378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541743-beast-can-beast-s-have-children?p=542191#post542191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;You wouldn't do the hanky panky upon Cthulhu would you?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally would.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;